      "line": null,
      "code": "const int is_frame_scaled =\n    cdef_info->allocated_mi_cols != cm->mi_params.mi_cols;\n...\nif (is_frame_scaled || is_sub_sampling_changed || is_cdef_flag_changed ||\n    is_large_scale_tile_changed || is_num_planes_changed ||\n    is_num_workers_changed)\n  av1_free_cdef_buffers(cm, cdef_worker, cdef_sync,\n                        cdef_info->allocated_num_workers);\n...\ncdef_info->allocated_mi_rows = num_mi_rows;",
      "note": "The staged patch adds an explicit `else if (cdef_info->allocated_mi_rows != num_mi_rows)` branch that frees and rebuilds `cdef_sync->cdef_row_mt`. In the vulnerable source, AddressSanitizer proves only that the crashing object was allocated at `alloccommon.c:199`; the smaller-earlier-allocation conclusion comes from source semantics, because both same-frame allocation here and later scheduling in `cdef_sb_row_worker_hook()` derive their row bounds from the current `cm->mi_params.mi_rows` with the same ceil(rows/64x64) formula. A row-sync array rebuilt for the later frame would therefore match the later schedule, so the saved overread requires a smaller earlier allocation to have remained live.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
